SINA_SMART["anat2-perineum"] = {"lecture":"anat2-perineum","title":"Perineum and pelvic floor","mapStatus":"auto: generated by universal.py from the lecture summary and key points; not human-reviewed","los":[{"id":"anat2-perineum:e0","text":"Pelvic floor: levator ani + coccygeus; separates pelvis from perineum.","topic":"The big picture","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"anat2-perineum:e1","text":"Functions: organ support, continence, sexual function.","topic":"The big picture","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"anat2-perineum:e9","text":"Weakness → prolapse and incontinence.","topic":"The big picture","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"anat2-perineum:e2","text":"Perineum: urogenital (anterior) and anal (posterior) triangles, divided at the ischial tuberosities.","topic":"Perineum: triangles and spaces","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"anat2-perineum:e3","text":"Superficial perineal space: ischiocavernosus, bulbospongiosus, superficial transverse perineal.","topic":"Perineum: triangles and spaces","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"anat2-perineum:e4","text":"Deep perineal space: external urethral sphincter, deep transverse perineal.","topic":"Perineum: triangles and spaces","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"anat2-perineum:e5","text":"Anal triangle: anal canal, external anal sphincter, ischioanal fossae.","topic":"Perineum: triangles and spaces","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"anat2-perineum:e6","text":"Perineal body: central attachment point.","topic":"Perineum: triangles and spaces","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"anat2-perineum:e7","text":"Levator ani: puborectalis, pubococcygeus, iliococcygeus.","topic":"Pelvic diaphragm and clinical points","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"anat2-perineum:e8","text":"Puborectalis sling: anorectal angle, faecal continence.","topic":"Pelvic diaphragm and clinical points","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"}],"vmap":{},"mlevel":{"cs5cre":"a","jpl4i8":"a","vzgenw":"a","t0h18e":"a","gc1knr":"a","dv0zn9":"a","1jtzeap":"a","px2yiq":"a","kb29en":"a","12eqaaw":"a"},"mapCounts":{"verified":0,"auto":10,"ambiguous":0,"missing":0},"mrules":[],"items":[],"experimental":[],"status":{},"difficulty":{},"expl":{"anat2-perineum:e0":{"s":0,"u":["Pelvic floor: levator ani + coccygeus; separates pelvis from perineum.","The pelvic floor separates the pelvic cavity from the perineum and is formed by muscles and fascia: the levator ani and coccygeus .","The perineum is the region of soft tissues below the pelvic diaphragm."],"dp":[]},"anat2-perineum:e1":{"s":0,"u":["Functions: organ support, continence, sexual function.","Functions: support of the pelvic organs , control of urination and defecation , and sexual function ."],"dp":[]},"anat2-perineum:e9":{"s":0,"u":["Weakness → prolapse and incontinence.","Clinical relevance: examination, pelvic organ prolapse and incontinence ."],"dp":[{"h":"Why childbirth can lead to prolapse years later","t":"During vaginal delivery the baby's head stretches the levator ani and the perineal body, and can tear them or injure the pudendal nerve. The damage may be silent at first, but with ageing and loss of oestrogen the weakened floor no longer supports the bladder, uterus and rectum against abdominal pressure, so they sag into the vagina. Pelvic floor exercises and repair of perineal tears aim to prevent this. Source: the lecture's clinical applications on prolapse and incontinence."}]},"anat2-perineum:e2":{"s":1,"u":["Perineum: urogenital (anterior) and anal (posterior) triangles, divided at the ischial tuberosities.","The diamond-shaped perineum, bounded by the pubic symphysis, ischiopubic rami, ischial tuberosities, sacrotuberous ligaments and coccyx, is divided by a line between the ischial tuberosities into the anterior urogenital triangle and the posterior anal triangle .","The anal triangle contains the anal canal, external anal sphincter and ischioanal fossae."],"dp":[{"h":"Note","t":"Perineum (diamond): a line between the ischial tuberosities divides it into the anterior urogenital and posterior anal triangles."}]},"anat2-perineum:e3":{"s":1,"u":["Superficial perineal space: ischiocavernosus, bulbospongiosus, superficial transverse perineal.","The urogenital perineum has layers: cutaneous plane, superficial perineal space (below the inferior fascia of the urogenital diaphragm, the perineal membrane) containing the ischiocavernosus , bulbospongiosus and superficial transverse perineal muscles with the erectile tissue (corpora cavernosa and spongiosum or clitoris and vestibular bulbs) and the greater vestibular glands; and the deep perineal space containing the external urethral sphincter (compressor urethrae and urethrovaginal sphincter in females) and the deep transverse perineal muscle , with the bulbourethral glands in males."],"dp":[{"h":"Note","t":"Superficial perineal space : ischiocavernosus, bulbospongiosus, superficial transverse perineal + erectile tissue + greater vestibular glands. Deep space : external urethral sphincter, deep transverse perineal, bulbourethral glands (male)."}]},"anat2-perineum:e4":{"s":1,"u":["Deep perineal space: external urethral sphincter, deep transverse perineal.","The urogenital perineum has layers: cutaneous plane, superficial perineal space (below the inferior fascia of the urogenital diaphragm, the perineal membrane) containing the ischiocavernosus , bulbospongiosus and superficial transverse perineal muscles with the erectile tissue (corpora cavernosa and spongiosum or clitoris and vestibular bulbs) and the greater vestibular glands; and the deep perineal space containing the external urethral sphincter (compressor urethrae and urethrovaginal sphincter in females) and the deep transverse perineal muscle , with the bulbourethral glands in males."],"dp":[]},"anat2-perineum:e5":{"s":1,"u":["Anal triangle: anal canal, external anal sphincter, ischioanal fossae.","The anal triangle contains the anal canal, external anal sphincter and ischioanal fossae.","The diamond-shaped perineum, bounded by the pubic symphysis, ischiopubic rami, ischial tuberosities, sacrotuberous ligaments and coccyx, is divided by a line between the ischial tuberosities into the anterior urogenital triangle and the posterior anal triangle ."],"dp":[{"h":"Clinical","t":"Ischioanal fossae (fat-filled, either side of the anal canal) can harbour abscesses that spread around the back (horseshoe abscess)."},{"h":"Note","t":"Internal anal sphincter = smooth, involuntary (autonomic); external anal sphincter = skeletal, voluntary ( pudendal nerve , inferior rectal branch)."}]},"anat2-perineum:e6":{"s":1,"u":["Perineal body: central attachment point.","The perineal body is the central fibromuscular point where these muscles converge."],"dp":[{"h":"Clinical","t":"The perineal body is the central anchor of the perineal muscles; tearing it in childbirth (or an episiotomy that extends) weakens support → prolapse and incontinence."}]},"anat2-perineum:e7":{"s":2,"u":["Levator ani: puborectalis, pubococcygeus, iliococcygeus.","The levator ani has three parts: puborectalis (a sling around the anorectal junction that maintains the anorectal angle, key for faecal continence), pubococcygeus and iliococcygeus ; with the coccygeus it forms the pelvic diaphragm, supporting the bladder, uterus and rectum and resisting rises in abdominal pressure."],"dp":[{"h":"Note","t":"Pelvic diaphragm = levator ani (puborectalis, pubococcygeus, iliococcygeus) + coccygeus; supplied by S3-S4 and the pudendal nerve."}]},"anat2-perineum:e8":{"s":2,"u":["Puborectalis sling: anorectal angle, faecal continence.","The levator ani has three parts: puborectalis (a sling around the anorectal junction that maintains the anorectal angle, key for faecal continence), pubococcygeus and iliococcygeus ; with the coccygeus it forms the pelvic diaphragm, supporting the bladder, uterus and rectum and resisting rises in abdominal pressure."],"dp":[{"h":"Clinical","t":"Puborectalis sling maintains the anorectal angle : key for faecal continence."}]}},"meta":{"cs5cre":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat2-perineum:e0/recall/1"},"jpl4i8":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat2-perineum:e0/recall/2"},"vzgenw":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat2-perineum:e2/recall/1"},"t0h18e":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat2-perineum:e3/recall/1"},"gc1knr":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat2-perineum:e4/recall/1"},"dv0zn9":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat2-perineum:e5/recall/1"},"1jtzeap":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat2-perineum:e6/recall/1"},"px2yiq":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat2-perineum:e7/recall/1"},"kb29en":{"a":"relationship","vg":"anat2-perineum:e9/relationship/1"},"12eqaaw":{"a":"recall","vg":"anat2-perineum:e3/recall/2"}},"explRev":"164594d149da"};
